WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.835
I put on a pretty dress
for you, Jimmy.

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.404
-You look gorgeous.
-What's up, fellas?

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.373
-Come on. It's so good to --
-So nice to be here.

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.874
Hi, everybody.
-Dude. I know, right?

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.075
Doesn't it feel good
to have the audience?

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.710
-I know. It's so weird.
-It's amazing.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.246
[ Cheers and applause ]
-And wonderful. Wonderful.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.613
-Thank you for doing the show.

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:16.616
We did the show, obviously,
from Zoom

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.718
when everyone was at home,
and I appreciate you doing that.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.819
But to see you in person,
I want to say congrats

00:00:20.819 --> 00:00:22.122
on so many things.
-Thank you.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.723
-"The Equalizer."
I mean, it's a giant hit.

00:00:24.723 --> 00:00:26.225
It's a smash. You're fantastic.

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.127
-Thank you, thank you,
thank you!

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.830
-I want to get into that,
but first, you were honored

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.999
with a BET Lifetime
Achievement Award,

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:35.535
and I want to say congrats
on that.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.503
-Thank you so much.
-Here's a picture of you.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:38.571
-Ah. Pops.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.006
-There's you and Pops
right there.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.640
-Me and Pops.
-I love your dad so much.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.609
-Hey, Dad!

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:47.279
-I just -- I just saw it, and,
honestly, I was like, "Whew."

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:49.149
'Cause if I didn't know if I --
I didn't want to get

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:50.983
too emotional,
but that's a big deal.

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:52.952
-I mean, yeah,
it kind of came out of nowhere,

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.520
and it was --

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.021
I was like, "For real?"
-'Cause I mean, that's --

00:00:56.021 --> 00:00:57.590
-I'm kind of young for
a lifetime achievement award.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.558
-Yeah, exactly. You have
so much more life to give.

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:01.761
Exactly. But, I mean, that's --
-Yeah, it was cool.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.729
-It's a good list of --
of people you're on.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:05.265
I mean, Prince --
I mean, you're on there

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.133
with a lot of awesome people.
-I know. That's what I said.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.367
I looked up the list,
and I'm like,

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.602
"Wow. This is crazy," you know?

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.737
-That was wild, but you
deserve it. It's awesome.

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:14.073
I like that you went on
with Pops,

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:15.808
but I also love
that you brought a --

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.544 line:0%
a photo of your mom.
-That's right.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:20.079 line:0%
I had to bring my mom with me.
Love you, Mommy.

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:22.047 line:0%
Yeah.
-She'd be so proud. Come on.

00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:23.316
-Yo, thank you, again.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.584
You know, our moms
look out for us, Jimmy.

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:27.020
You got to always know that.
-Yup.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.589
-Jimmy sent me shepherd's pie.
You sent me shepherd's pie.

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:32.058
You know, I lost my mom, and --

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:34.561
and all of a sudden,
this delivery comes to the door.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:37.129
And I'm like, "What is that?"
You know?

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:39.399
-Yeah, yeah. What are you --
-What is --

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.666
And it was food from Jimmy.

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:42.635
Jimmy sent me a bunch
of shepherd's pie.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:45.171
And I'm like, "That's so weird."
-I didn't know what to do.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.705
-Man, we smashed
that shepherd's pie!

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:48.107
-Right.
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:50.776
-I didn't know that
we would need so much food!

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:53.446
We tore that shepherd's pie up.
So thank you, again.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.881
Everybody needed that,
and you are the best.

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:57.650
-I love you. I love you.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.986
I heard that you just did
a movie with Adam Sandler.

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:02.988
Is that true?
-Yes. I love -- Man.

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:04.323
-How was --
How was Adam Sandler?

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:05.925
He's the greatest.
-Adam Sandler is so --

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.393
-You guys together?
I'm going to freak out.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:10.263
-We were in Philly, too.
I mean, it was crazy. Yes.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.331
We -- We did a movie
called "Hustle."

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:14.934
I cannot wait for you all
to see it.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.370
My dream came true.
I play Adam's wife.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.372
-Yes!
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:20.372 --> 00:02:23.008
-Yes. I've had a quest.
-Those are the best things.

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:25.144
-He is the best,
and it was just so much fun

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:27.080
working with him
and just, like --

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.382
You know, he's carrying around
a bucket of music, you know?

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:32.418
It's just like this bucket box
of sound and --

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.220
-And he's just walking
around having --

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.421
-He's a sweetheart.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.189
Just having fun
and making everybody happy.

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:38.591
-Which is the key, right?
-Yeah.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.659
-That's the key to anything.
-And it's so different

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:41.961
from what I do
on "The Equalizer."

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:44.697
I'm, like, going hard all day.
Like -- [ Grunting ]

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.299
You know?
-And then I get to like, "Ah."

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:48.835
-Yeah, but you --
-Adam Sandler.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.736
-You get to -- By the way --
-A movie set.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:52.271
-You're crushing
on "The Equalizer."

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:53.639
I love it.
Do you like doing it?

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.008
I mean, all this crazy --
-I do.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.475
-I mean, you're good at it.

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:59.011
-Well, finally,
those, uh, gunslinging skills

00:02:59.011 --> 00:03:00.380
I've been working on
all my life...

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.714
-Yeah, it paid off. Exactly.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:05.051
-...karate.
-Yes.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.785
-But let's talk --

00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:09.656
It premiered
after the Super Bowl.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:12.692
The biggest ratings in, like,
10 years or something crazy.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.627
Number-one show
for the whole year.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.562
-Yeah. Thank you, thank you.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:17.730
For making it number one.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.032
-And it's fantastic.
-You can do it again.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:20.899
-And great reviews.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.899 --> 00:03:23.836
-You said the show
was a role of a lifetime.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:26.005
What can fans expect
for season two?

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:30.243
-They can expect the same
action, emotion, tension.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.178
Fun. A fun ride.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:33.813
Just a good fun ride
for an hour.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.948
-It really is.
-And some justice, you know?

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:37.683
And that's the best part
about be--

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:40.019
you know, playing this character
in "The Equalizer."

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.721
I get to, like, mete justice,

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:45.024
make sure that the good people
get what they deserve, you know,

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.493
and -- and people
who can't help themselves get --

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.495
get a good shake, so --
-You get to do everything.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.798
-And I get to do it,
while, you know, gunslingin'.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:54.500
And cracking backs!

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.637
-Cracking backs. Come on.
It is great, though.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.905
And I watch it,
and I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:03:59.905 --> 00:04:01.473
It's just perfect.
I'm so happy for you.

00:04:01.473 --> 00:04:02.875
I want to show a clip.

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.610
Here's Queen Latifah in season
two of "The Equalizer."

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.145
Take a look.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:09.915
-Oh, we got a few texts on
the board that deserve a look.

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:13.185
Word on the alt net is
that you are a real-life hero.

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:15.721
Your legend is growing.

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:19.659
-Yeah, that's a problem.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.627
I'm too exposed.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:25.397
When I was working overseas,
no one knew who I was.

00:04:25.397 --> 00:04:27.900
Now my legend has grown
all the way to the DA's office.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.502
Cops know about me.

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.537
Delilah does, too?

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:32.838
Maybe I was foolish thinking

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:36.442
I could do this work
so close to home.

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:39.011
I don't know, guys.
Maybe it's time we stop.

00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:43.449
♪♪

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.417
-Yeah.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:47.119
Queen Latifah, everybody.

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:50.423
Season two of "The Equalizer"
premieres this Sunday.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.091
-Whoo!
-This Sunday.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.927
Set your DVR. Set your TiVos.

